# Remote Command Logic

## Flow
1. EMM UI/API → `POST /api/mqtt/{mqttUsername}/command` → DB row `pending` → publish MQTT → `sent`.
2. Agent `on_emm_message` parses JSON → looks up `ASYNC_COMMAND_HANDLERS[action]` first, else `COMMAND_HANDLERS[action]`.
3. Sync handlers run on the Paho callback thread and return `(success, message)` for immediate ACK.
4. Async handlers (today: `DOWNLOAD_LOGS`) are submitted to `command_executor` (dedicated pool, `max_workers=1`); **no ACK until the job finishes**.
5. Agent publishes ACK on `charger/{user}/response`.
6. EMM subscriber updates `mqtt_command.status` / `message`.

## Envelope (inbound)
```json
{
  "commandId": "cmd_…",
  "action": "START_CHARGING",
  "payload": { "deviceUid": "002544" },
  "timestamp": "…"
}
```

## ACK (outbound)
```json
{
  "commandId": "cmd_…",
  "action": "START_CHARGING",
  "status": "success",
  "message": "Spuštění nabíjení bylo úspěšně vyžádáno pro nabíjecí bod 002544",
  "timestamp": "2026-03-13T08:36:47"
}
```
- `message` is Czech, short, operator-facing.
- Unknown `action` → ACK `failed` (do not crash).
- Never put archive bytes or binary fields on MQTT.

## Implemented handlers (`COMMAND_HANDLERS` — sync)
| Action | Needs `deviceUid` | Local effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `RESTART` | yes | `POST .../charging-controllers/{uid}/restart` |
| `FORCE_LEDS` | yes | Toggle `force_leds` via GET then PUT control |
| `START_CHARGING` | yes | Require IEC state in B/C/D family; PUT `external_release/locking/charge_enable` |
| `STOP_CHARGING` | yes | Require connected state; PUT release off / unlock |
| `UPDATE_SETTINGS` | yes | Map camelCase payload `settings` → snake_case; PUT charging-point config |

Always call `validate_controller(payload)` first for controller-scoped actions.

### Settings key map (EMM → Phoenix)
`chargingPointName`→`charging_point_name`, `location`→`location`, `releaseChargingMode`→`release_charging_mode`, `minimumChargeCurrent`→`minimum_charge_current`, `maximumChargeCurrent`→`maximum_charge_current`, `fallbackChargeCurrent`→`fallback_charge_current`.

## Implemented async handlers (`ASYNC_COMMAND_HANDLERS`)
| Action | Needs `deviceUid` | Local effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `DOWNLOAD_LOGS` | no (charger-level) | WBM login (`webUsername`/`webPassword` from payload) → GET log pack → HTTPS multipart upload to `{EMM_HOST}/api/v2/public/charger-logs` (`commandId` + Bearer ApiKey) → ACK. Archive never on MQTT. Runs on `command_executor`. |

WBM credentials come only from the MQTT payload — never write them to logs or `charging_data.conf`. FW branching for WBM HTTP vs HTTPS lives in `charx_website.py`.

